WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.163
In his later years, Emperor Qianlong trusted Heshen deeply.

00:00:03.163 --> 00:00:06.460
Heshen was clever and capable, and his power grew greater and greater.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:09.230
All the ministers knew that Heshen enjoyed the emperor's favor most.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.940
The large mansion he lived in was even more luxurious than a prince's palace.

00:00:12.987 --> 00:00:16.059
His storehouses were piled full of gold, silver, and treasures.

00:00:16.059 --> 00:00:18.995
He smiled smugly, his eyes narrowing into slits.

00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:22.383
Much of this wealth had been obtained through corruption.

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:27.258
In 1799, Emperor Qianlong passed away.

00:00:27.258 --> 00:00:31.065
The new emperor, Emperor Jiaqing, immediately ordered an investigation of him.

00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:33.870
Officials counting his assets were shocked.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.330
Emperor Jiaqing's orders came one after another.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.530
The wealth confiscated from him was astonishingly vast.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.570
He was dismissed from office and ordered to take his own life, an end that left people sighing.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:48.192
The inventory work went on for many days before it was finished.

00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:50.817
Because of this, a saying spread among the people.

00:00:50.902 --> 00:00:54.466
It went: When Heshen falls, Jiaqing eats his fill.
